  "id": "Compound::DB00713 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Oxacillin, a penicillin antibiotic, is linked to Slc15a1 through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on the Penicillin class of antibiotics. The evidence suggests that Oxacillin, through its structural resemblance to other penicillins like Cyclacillin and Azidocillin, binds to Slc15a1, a protein involved in transport processes. This binding is supported by the shared pathway involving Penicillin Antibiotic, indicating a broader functional relationship within the penicillin family. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism where Oxacillin, as a penicillin, exerts its effects via a common molecular mechanism, which is then extended to other penicillins through structural and functional similarity. The presence of multiple low common ancestors reinforces the centrality of Penicillin in this relationship, suggesting a conserved biological role across related antibiotics.",
